    "created_at": "2025-10-25T11:05:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-25T11:05:31Z",
    "body": "Made another iteration to address the concern from @annevk Now, the test first loads the `red.png` (to ensure the event handler is compiled for this). Then, after the iframe has loaded, we update the image to load `green.png`, triggering the `onload` once again.\n\nHere, if the `iframe1.remove()` is removed, Chrome passes. Yet with that line, the test fails in Chrome. That doesn't seem correct to me, since the element was already moved to `frame0document` and therefore `iframe1` should no longer be a factor for its event handlers.\n\nFirefox passes all four tests, but 7/10 time out on \"Event handler IDL attributes must point window to the element's document's global\": https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/55454/checks?check_run_id=53651005269 That is also strange to me, since we set the `src` after we add the `load` listener. Therefore, it should have run like normal?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
